					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-174999#post-4001346</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-174999/reddawn#post-4001346</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 24 Sep 2018 02:51:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Xoloitzcuintli</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2911394</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I know some people are complaining that it's too offensive in depiction of Russians, but I say lighten up a little. Sure, the humor today is a lot more watered down and less funny than it used to be, but I still consider it a good read. It's fiction above all, and frankly, even if not Russian myself, I myself wouldn't even be too offended if someone gave me the most crude depiction of America in the form of a character, Foundation or otherwise. Upvoting because I love the style of it and the crude humor is right up my alley.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
